 JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed in `README.md`.

+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request carries `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are stored in the
+data as `apiKeys: [{ "key", "name", "role" }]`.
+
+- No key, or a key that is not known: `401` with code `unauthorized`.
+- A known key whose role may not call the route: `403` with code `forbidden`.
+
+| Role      | May call                                                                 |
+| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
+| `viewer`  | every `GET` route except `GET /audit`                                    |
+| `cook`    | as `viewer`, plus `POST /recipes/:id/cook`, `POST /batches/:id/waste`, `POST /temperatures`, `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts` |
+| `manager` | everything                                                               |
+
+## Audit
+
+Every request that may change data (any method but `GET`) made with a known
+key writes an audit entry `{ id, at, keyName, method, path, status }`,
+whatever its outcome (refused requests are logged with `403`).
+`GET /audit` lists the entries newest first; it is for managers only.
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
